        "date": "2026-11-19T01:44:14Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): cut a level at the tab top so a contour tab is tab_height tall\n\nA closed-ring 2D Contour carries its tabs on each level below\nbottom_z + tab_height. The last level above that plane cut the whole\nring, so a tab stood up to that level: 4 mm with a 4 mm stepdown and a\n1.5 mm tab height.\n\nContourParams::ring_levels adds the tab top as a level when the\nstepdown ladder has none there. A level within 1e-6 mm of the tab top\nbecomes the tab top itself (0.2 mm steps gave -3.0000000000000004, a\nlevel under the tab top that carried the tabs). The closed contour and\nthe whole-model contour read ring_levels. The open runs have no tabs\nand keep levels.\n\nPins: crates/motion/tests/contour_tab_height.rs measures the tab height\nfrom the posted moves for a stepdown larger and smaller than the tab\nheight. Four old pins and the first-router-part example follow the\nadded pass.\n\nFixes #2579\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "ae1ff8cc30b7f67307521a236e8d5c5741fe6565",
